# Homeopathic Dermatology Clinical Framework & AI Evaluation Hub

## 🩺 Overview
This repository features specialized clinical data, repertorial analysis, and AI prompt evaluation rubrics dedicated exclusively to dermatological conditions (such as Eczema, Psoriasis, Acne Vulgaris, Urticaria, and chronic skin eruptions). Drawing from active clinical homeopathic practice in dermatology since 2016, this project bridges traditional skin case management with modern Artificial Intelligence (AI) evaluation and data annotation standards.

## 🌟 Key Focus Areas
* **Specialized Skin Care Practice:** Documenting and structuring chronic and acute dermatological cases with detailed evaluation of local and general modalities, sensations, and skin-specific aggravations/ameliorations.
* **Repertorial Mapping for Dermatology:** Applying classical homeopathic principles to map skin symptoms and lesion characteristics into clean, machine-readable JSON formats.
* **AI Domain Expertise & Prompt Design:** Designing specialized prompt engineering templates and evaluation metrics to test Large Language Models (LLMs) on dermatological reasoning, edge cases, and medical safety boundaries.

## 📂 Repository Structure
- `datasets/` : Anonymized dermatology case studies and specific repertory rubrics for skin disorders (JSON/CSV).
- `prompts/` : Specialized prompt engineering templates designed for testing LLMs on dermatological case analysis.
- `evaluation_rubrics/` : Quality assurance metrics for assessing AI-generated medical explanations and safety compliance.

